  "habitat": "Dry woodland and thornveld, including mopane and other broad-leaved or acacia bush, more uniform cover than the Lilac-breasted Roller uses.",
  "summary": "A large resident roller with a square tail, a white eyebrow, olive-green upperparts, and deep purple underparts streaked white. Southern birds, including those in Kruger, have the olive-green crown rather than a rufous one. The sexes are not separately described. The immature is duller, without part-by-part colours in the sources used here, and the chick is not described. Some birds move locally, and the northern Transvaal is named as a wintering area for part of the regional population.",
